 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The damsel of the Isaurian mountain\nHer youth is golden, and her youth appears\nThe first bliss to all by education born;\nBut she with a trembling tenderness,\nLike some unmarred sunbeam fallen,\nYet finds satisfaction in herself;\nFor when he that led this habitant through\nThese steps hath been gone no more, alone\nShe has a thought as beautiful still,\nThat may be the life of others still.\nThey who know that a day was turn'd away,\nA thing without which nothing remains,",
